  "description": "The 100 highest named peaks in Washington State, from Mount Rainier down to roughly 8,320 ft, compiled by John Lixvar and John Plimpton in 1976.",
  "criteria": "The 100 highest summits in Washington, ranked by USGS-quad elevation. The list generally follows a 400 ft prominence guideline but includes exceptions (e.g. Seven Fingered Jack, Sahale, Dark, Rahm, Horseshoe, Little Annapurna have under 400 ft); the stricter prominence-only variant is the separate 'Washington Top 100'.",
  "organization": "Informal (originated with John Lixvar & John Plimpton; Mountaineers branches award badges)",
  "officialUrl": "https://www.peakbagger.com/list.aspx?lid=5003",
  "notes": "Ranks and elevations follow rhinoclimbs.com (USGS quad elevations, post-1980 Mount St. Helens). A trailing '+' in the source means a contour-based minimum, recorded here as the integer with a note. Lists vary between sources and updated lidar/dGPS surveys (countryhighpoints.com) change the tail end of the list. Ranges are a coarse grouping added by the compiler; lat/lon included only for the five volcanoes (from Wikipedia). Mount Rainier is the source's 14,410 ft; Liberty Cap is not a separate entry.",
